{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/501853-playing-ultra-psions","id":501853,"title":"Playing Ultra-Psions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-03T10:14:41-07:00","id":501853,"title":"Playing Ultra-Psions","content":"Did anyone else have the itch to play someone who had some dots in every Aptitude? Or was that just me?<br /> It is not that I had this itch to be a minmaxer. I had already outgrown that. But I had always envisioned playing a psionically gifted person who had a lot of even the most basic things (like maybe one or two dots at best) in each of the Aptitudes. It always got in my craw that I could not get more than one Aptitude. I do understand the reasoning behind it. One, XP-prohibitive. Two, it was also Psi point prohibitive since there was such a small pool of Psi to use to do your effects. Third, it would make a character unbearably powerful after a long enough game. Lastly, I understand that the Doyen crippled humanity. I get all of these. I do. But the itch was always there to branch out. I know that the Venezualan Phenomenon would also have allowed it, if the book had been published. I wish it had been, though. *wipes up the drool*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T14:05:41-07:00","id":502152,"title":"","content":"what you're talking about are what they call &quot;Psiads&quot; and they gave the rules (however minimalist) for them in the Aberrant Player's Guide. They're a footnote in the series since they are naturally-occurring Psions, but yeah I've played one of those. The only thing they can't get is Quantakinetics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T19:24:59-07:00","id":502386,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything wrong with it, personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T19:27:28-07:00","id":503730,"title":"","content":"I don't either. I have placed my Trinity stories on hold while waiting for the new edition to be published. I have 2 new players and a possible 3rd so it makes sense to hold off on running new stories.<br /> I have seen a campaign with Psiads and didn't see any issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:54:31-07:00","id":503864,"title":"","content":"I never got a chance to play one. I did get a chance to NPC one, though. I used him in an Aberrant game. He had come back in time to kill some of the key players in the Esperanza crash...ie the players. After they defeated him (which was rough since I went with the fact that Psi &gt; Quantum. Yes, it was my early days and I have gotten a bit better at interpretation of things), they then had to deal with the fact that they were keenly aware of the Aberrant War and that they did something big in it. <br /> But getting back to my own point, I always envisioned Psions who had some splashes of each Aptitude. I do hope that the rules allow for something akin to it, even if it is hard as all get out to obtain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T23:08:00-07:00","id":503869,"title":"","content":"I ran a deliberately over-powered Huang-Marr biorg against a party of tainted 2120 Aberrants, while that one biorg didn't have dots in <i>every</i> mode, they weren't restricted. But that was all house-rules and non-canon, so i'm not sure how much it counts. I ran them with the free-form Psi rules and even missing a few aptitudes, the breadth of possibilities each turn were staggering.<br /> Rules-wise, Psiads as they were presented offered this kind of cross-aptitude selection, but tended to be less powerful than chamber-psions, who gained the extra kicker due to the noetic restrictions on their abilities. At least as far as i remember (perhaps falsely).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:27:14-07:00","id":511860,"title":"","content":"As an aside, what kind of complication may it bring to the Trinity setting if a n unintended number of Psiads if still around due to subtle but quite active &quot;Prometheus draft-dodging&quot; underground movement, or something along those lines, lead by some conspiracy theorists (&quot;wasn't Utopia also involved with fitting Aberrants in society? See where did that get us&quot; discourse kind of people, for an example) and a whole variety of other paranoid or authority-distrusting sort of folks?<br /> <br /> It could serve as a nice &quot;sometimes antagonist, sometimes ally&quot; kind of organization (supposing there's only one) in a game, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Not to mention crazy twists if Adventure's <b>Daredevils</b> are still around and kicking, be them another brand of evolved human or &quot;just&quot; groups of hyper-competent baseline humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T01:34:46-07:00","id":513966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nihilist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/501853-playing-ultra-psions?p=503869#post503869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .Rules-wise, Psiads as they were presented offered this kind of cross-aptitude selection, but tended to be less powerful than chamber-psions, who gained the extra kicker due to the noetic restrictions on their abilities. At least as far as i remember (perhaps falsely).</div> </div> </div> </div>Weren't the psiads limited to four dots in each aptitude? I seem to remember that was the trade-off - psiads could learn almost anything, but couldn't reach the fifth level in any of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T05:44:16-07:00","id":514063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/501853-playing-ultra-psions?p=513966#post513966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the psiads limited to four dots in each aptitude? I seem to remember that was the trade-off - psiads could learn almost anything, but couldn't reach the fifth level in any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you mention it that sounds familiar. A quick check vinidcates you loosely, you've glossed over the details, but that's essentially how it works. Most Psiads can't ever go above three in each mode, only those with 9-10 Psi can ever learn level four modes. They can spend experience to raise any mode, even those outside of their primary aptitudes (plural) including Teleportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4458,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","user":"Nihilist","date":".  nobody really cares why i edited - feel free to devise your own reasons, i'll play along 05-14-2015, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T15:50:56-07:00","id":549463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/501853-playing-ultra-psions?p=513966#post513966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't the psiads limited to four dots in each aptitude? I seem to remember that was the trade-off - psiads could learn almost anything, but couldn't reach the fifth level in any of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Four dots max in their two specialty styles (PK and EK for kinetics, forex), three dots in everything else. Teleporters only got the three abilities in Upeo Wa Macho. I'd still love to run a psiad-oriented campaign, though I'd probably just call them psions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Heroes die. Hope is a phoenix.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2434-captain-aeon","name":"Captain Aeon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2434_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"203"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}